## Installing

Clone it into the `libraries` folder of your sketchbook, under the name `{{ project_name }}`:

```bash
git clone {{ url }} ~/Arduino/libraries/{{ project_name }}
```

It is built and checked for `{{ fqbn }}`.

## Using it

```cpp
#include <{{ project_name }}.h>

void setup() { Serial.begin(115200); }

void loop() {
  Serial.println({{ namespace }}::Clamp(analogRead(A0), 100, 900));
  delay(1000);
}
```

The examples in [examples/](examples) show more; the reference is built from the Doxygen blocks
of `src/`, see [docs/Documentation.md](docs/Documentation.md).

## Developing

The dev container in [.devcontainer/](.devcontainer/README.md) carries every tool. The checks,
which CI runs on each pull request as well:

```bash
tools/lint.sh                       # clang-format, cpplint, shellcheck, actionlint; --fix formats
tools/tidy.sh                       # clang-tidy, with the board's flags and on the tests
tools/cppcheck.sh                   # cppcheck on the library
cmake --workflow --preset default   # the tests on the host
cmake --workflow --preset sanitize  # under ASan and UBSan
tools/coverage.sh                   # the tests, and what they reach of src/
tools/self_check.sh                 # examples/SelfCheck in simavr
tools/compile_examples.sh           # every example in each variant, fails on a warning
tools/docs.sh                       # the reference, fails on a gap
```

The checks, the CI and the dev container come from the
[template](https://github.com/theAndreas/embedded-cpp-template); `uvx copier update`
brings its newest version. What is the project's own for them lies in `tools/project.sh`.

